Write a function to find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings. Here are the unit tests: 
// longestCommonPrefix({"flower","flow","flight"}) should return "fl" 
// longestCommonPrefix({"dog","racecar","car"}) should return "" 
// longestCommonPrefix({"interview","intermediate","internal","internet"}) should return "inter"

answer:
To find the longest common prefix among an array of strings, you can compare each string character by character from the start until a mismatch is found. Here's a function that accomplishes this:

```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <string>

std::string longestCommonPrefix(std::vector<std::string>& strs) {
    if (strs.empty()) return "";

    for (size_t i = 0; i < strs[0].length(); ++i) {
        char c = strs[0][i];
        for (size_t j = 1; j < strs.size(); ++j) {
            if (i == strs[j].length() || strs[j][i] != c) {
                return strs[0].substr(0, i);
            }
        }
    }
    return strs[0];
}
```

This function starts by checking the first string character by character. For each character, it compares with the corresponding position in all other strings. If a mismatch is found, it returns the substring up to that point. If all strings match up to the end of the shortest string, that substring is returned.

